  "final_text": "I fixed the format-spec parser in `youtube_dl/YoutubeDL.py`, in `_parse_format_selection`. `test_youtube_format_selection` now passes, along with the other 13 tests in `test/test_YoutubeDL.py`.\n\nAfter handling a `/` choice, the parser added the choice to the selector list and set `current_selector` to `None`. A following `,` then added that `None` to the list. That crashed specs like `bestvideo/best,bestaudio` with `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'type'`.\n\nThe parser now keeps the choice as `current_selector`, so the `,` or the end of the spec adds it once."
